{
  "$comment": "Spine key fixtures, version v1 (OSE-1615). Names in, ids out. Any repository that computes these keys must reproduce every row. Rule: .telemetry/tracking-plan.md, Decisions 1 and 2. Hashes here were computed with node:crypto, independently of src/lib/spine-keys.ts.",
  "version": "v1",
  "hash": "first 32 lower-case hex characters of SHA-256 over the UTF-8 bytes; fields joined with |",
  "venue_input": "v1|<normalised name>|<res-7 cell, trimmed, lower case>",
  "event_input": "v1|<venue_canonical_id>|<uec_code, trimmed>|<bucket>",
  "normalise": "in order: (1) remove apostrophes (' U+2019 U+2018 U+02BC ` U+00B4); (2) Unicode NFKC; (3) lower-case with the Unicode lower-case mapping, locale-independent (JavaScript toLowerCase, Python str.lower), NOT case folding, then put the result in Unicode NFC; (4) remove apostrophes again; (5) remove variation selectors (U+FE00 to U+FE0F, U+E0100 to U+E01EF), enclosing marks (general category Me) and format characters (general category Cf: the soft hyphen, zero-width spaces and joiners); (6) & becomes ' and ' (with a space each side); (7) every run of characters whose general category is not a letter (L*), a mark (M*) or a number (N*: Nd, Nl and No) becomes one space (U+0020); (8) remove any run of marks that stands at the start or directly after a space; (9) collapse runs of spaces to one and remove a space at either end; (10) if the name now begins with 'the ' (the word and one space), drop those four characters, once; (11) remove a space at either end. An empty result gives no key.",
  "bucket": "the local calendar date of starts_at in the event's zone, minus one day when the local wall-clock time is before 04:00. The zone is the one stored on the event; when it is missing, or the implementation's time-zone database does not know it, America/Chicago is used (OSE only stores a zone its own runtime accepted, so an implementation with an older or stricter database can disagree for such a zone). starts_at counts only when it is an instant: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM, optionally :SS and a fraction, then Z or an offset written +HH:MM or -HH:MM. Anything else (no zone, a date alone, a year alone, text) is not an instant. When there is no starts_at, or it is not an instant, the bucket is the first ten characters of start_date, which must be a real calendar date written YYYY-MM-DD; otherwise there is no bucket.",
  "type_code": "uec_code trimmed, case kept; empty or 'unknown' (any case) gives no key",
  "unicode": "Generated with Unicode 17.0 (Node 24.14.1). NFKC is stable for assigned characters. A general category can differ between Unicode versions for newly assigned characters, so an implementation on an older Unicode version that disagrees with a row should look at that row's newest character first (the emoji rows are the likeliest). In review on 2026-10-12 two implementations written only from the words in this file, one in Node and one in Python 3.11 (Unicode 14.0), reproduced the 84 rows the file then had; the rows and steps added after that (format characters, NFC, the instant rule) have been checked against this repository's function only.",
